From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:44:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: check remote EVPN neighbours in kernel MAC external
 learn mode

New topotest bgp_evpn_ext_learn_rem_neigh: two VTEPs in MAC external
learn mode share an L2-VNI and a host that sits behind one of them. The
other VTEP must install the host's IPv4 and IPv6 neighbours in the
kernel as remote (NOARP, extern_learn), keep them remote when it routes
to the host, follow the host when it moves from one VTEP to the other
and back, follow the IPv4 address when a host with another MAC takes it
over, and remove them when the MAC/IP routes are withdrawn.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
